### 3. Cybersecurity Framework

#### 3.1. Security Policies

Cybersecurity is a top priority for TechWave Solutions. Our security policies were last updated in March 2023 and include guidelines for data protection, incident reporting, and employee training. The policies are enforced by our Chief Information Security Officer (CISO), Robert Martinez, who leads a dedicated cybersecurity team.

Annual security awareness training is mandatory for all employees and is conducted by an external provider, CyberSafe Solutions, to ensure best practices in data handling and phishing prevention.

#### 3.2. Risk Assessment

We conduct bi-annual risk assessments to identify vulnerabilities within our IT infrastructure. The most recent assessment, completed in September 2023 by SecureTech Consultants, highlighted potential risks in our legacy systems. As a result, a phased approach to upgrade those systems is set to begin in Q1 2024.

#### 3.3. Incident Response Plan

Our Incident Response Plan (IRP) was drafted in collaboration with CyberDefense Group and outlines procedures for responding to potential security breaches. The plan includes immediate containment measures, communication protocols, and post-incident analysis. The IRP was successfully tested in a tabletop exercise in August 2023, involving key stakeholders from IT, HR, and Legal departments.

